<p>NOTE: The company uses a supplemental performance measure along with net earnings (loss) to report its operating results.  This measure, Earnings Before Depreciation and Deferred Taxes (EBDDT), is not a measure of operating results or cash flows from operating activities as defined by generally accepted accounting principles. Additionally, EBDDT is not necessarily indicative of cash available to fund cash needs and should not be considered as an alternative to cash flows as a measure of liquidity.  However, the Company believes that EBDDT provides relevant information about its operations and is necessary, along with net earnings (loss), for an understanding of its operating results. Depreciation, amortization and deferred income taxes are excluded from EBDDT as they represent non-cash charges.  Gains on the sale of non-strategic land and other assets represent nonrecurring items and are therefore excluded from EBDDT.</p>
